course: dictionary
lesson: 1881
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word collection is a good example. In «As the collection plate went past in church in Boston», collection does not mean a set of stamps. It means the plate that gathers money.
explain: Ask what the word is doing in the sentence. If the sentence is about things a person keeps, like «a stamp collection», then collection is a group of things gathered and owned. If it is about taking rubbish away, then collection means the act of collecting.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «In Houston, Aaliyah's little sisters wreck her slime collection.» Her slime collection is the slime she has gathered and keeps, so her sisters are spoiling things that belong to her.
fact: A collection is a group of things a person gathers and keeps, like stamps or shells.
fact: A collection can also mean the act of collecting, as in «rubbish collection».
fact: A collection can be stories, songs or art kept together, as in a museum.
fact: A collection plate in church gathers money given to the church.
fact: Use the sentence to choose the meaning: the words around collection tell you which one is right.
exercise: «In Houston, Aaliyah's little sisters wreck her slime collection.» What does collection mean here? | *A group of things she gathers and keeps | The act of taking rubbish away | A plate passed round in church | A museum of old songs
exercise: What is the collection plate for in church? | Keeping old stories safe | *Gathering money given to the church | Cleaning the seats | Carrying food to the kitchen
exercise: Which sentence uses collection to mean the act of collecting? | *«Rubbish collection is on Monday morning.» | «The museum has a fine collection of paintings.» | «Her shell collection sits on the shelf.» | «Add a new stamp to your collection.»
test: «Writing is not a test on one day: your teacher looks at a collection of your work from across the year.» What does collection mean here? | Money given to charity | A plate passed round in church | *A group of your work kept together | The act of collecting rubbish
test: A collection can grow or shrink. Which of these makes a collection grow? | Giving things away | Losing things in the park | *Finding or buying more | Throwing them in the bin
exam: In «a collection for charity», what does collection mean? | *The act of gathering money from people | A shell shop | A stamp album | A set of stories in a library
